# Switch long equality chains

When four or more branches compare the same value for equality, use a `switch`
instead of an `if` / `else if` chain.

```typescript
// Avoid
if (stage === 'draw') handleDraw()
else if (stage === 'discard') handleDiscard()
else if (stage === 'sacrifice') handleSacrifice()
else if (stage === 'search') handleSearch()

// Prefer
switch (stage) {
  case 'draw':
    return handleDraw()
  case 'discard':
    return handleDiscard()
  case 'sacrifice':
    return handleSacrifice()
  case 'search':
    return handleSearch()
}
```

Keep guards as `if` statements when branches test different expressions,
ranges, or compound conditions rather than one shared discriminant.
